1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:19,514
Marcellus arrived with the Crown of Midnight, a clean jacket, and a
grievance. "You might have left me one mirror." I looked around the
ruined hall. Glass everywhere. Reflection in installments. "Nigga, you
look excellent." "That is not the same as checking." Shawna opened her
compact for him.

2
00:00:19,764 --> 00:00:43,709
He adjusted his collar, thanked her, and set the case on the one table
we hadn't personally reduced to a suggestion. Gold. Dark stones. Old
workmanship. Men had ruined their whole lives trying to get that thing
onto their heads. Now Marcellus lifted it toward mine with the
cautious expression of a nigga adding a chandelier to a room already
on fire.

3
00:00:43,959 --> 00:01:08,327
"Stand still." "I am." "Your mouth is moving." Tank made a noise
behind me. I ignored that nigga with dignity. The crown settled.
Marcellus stepped back. Tank looked at me, then at the crown, then at
me again. "Nigga." "What?" "That's a lot of you at once." Cassius put
a hand over his heart. "My brother, we need a larger painting." Victor
folded his arms.

4
00:01:08,577 --> 00:01:33,495
"The academy already discusses his cheekbones in meetings. This will
require a committee." "Tell those niggas the cheeks remain available
by appointment." Shawna stepped close. She studied the crown, shifted
it slightly to one side, then leaned back. "There." "Better?" "More
you. Unfortunately for everybody else." I kissed her. Behind us, one
palace guard whispered to another.

5
00:01:33,745 --> 00:01:57,488
"Nigga looks born in it." "The emperor thinks he's about to be the
tallest thing in the room." "Nigga hasn't seen this." I turned. "Speak
up. A compliment shouldn't need protection." Both niggas straightened.
Tank closed his eyes. My wife covered her face with the hand that had
just arranged my crown, as if she could withdraw her contribution
retroactively.

6
00:01:57,738 --> 00:02:20,129
"You will be impossible all afternoon." "Baby, I cleared the evening
too." Marcellus shut the empty case. "If you are finished admiring
yourself, there is an emperor." "Nigga, I'm capable of disappointing
him and enjoying myself simultaneously." Shawna took my hand. I
stopped looking for reflections and looked where we were going.

7
00:02:20,379 --> 00:02:42,183
The midnight court stood beyond the ruined hall, at the center of the
inner palace. Its doors were black wood inlaid with stars. Two guards
opened them when Vesper approached, and for the first time since
entering the fortress, nobody immediately tried to shoot us. I
appreciated a room willing to establish a little suspense.

8
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:51,341
The court was round, with a glass dome above and a floor of black
marble. Seats rose in a circle around a central platform.

9
00:02:51,591 --> 00:03:15,401
Men and women filled them: officers, merchants, old criminal rulers,
palace favorites, people who had come because Zero ordered it and
people who had stayed because they wanted to see what happened when
the nigga everyone talked about finally stood in front of the man who
owned the talking. Zero waited on the platform. A sword hung at his
side. Nigga, finally.

10
00:03:15,651 --> 00:03:37,640
Something honest about the invitation. He watched me enter wearing the
crown. I saw the moment the sight hurt him. He hid it quickly. He was
good at that. But I had spent too long loving a woman with a dead
man's watch on her wrist to miss the exact place a man's pride could
bruise beneath a calm face. "Captain," he said.

11
00:03:37,890 --> 00:04:04,810
"Emperor." "The crown suits your appetite." "Nigga, everything suits
me. You picked an inconvenient enemy." A few people laughed before
catching themselves. Zero heard them. So did I. My people spread along
the court's lower seats. Shawna stayed at my right. Tank at my left.
Vesper stood behind us with the folio. Marcellus took a seat beside
Magnolia, the empty crown case on his knees.

12
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:29,866
Knox remained near the doors with Noor and Salma. Cassius, Inez,
Victor, Seraphine, Rosa, Mercedes, Porsche, June, Adrian,
Liora—everybody who had crossed a road or a sky to reach this room
found a place where they could see me. Nigga, if the emperor wanted an
audience, I had brought the part that mattered. Zero raised one hand.
The room quieted.

13
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:52,531
"You have heard stories of this man," he said. "You have watched him
seize cars, command officers, entertain crowds, and name himself king.
You have mistaken spectacle for permanence." "Nigga, I been permanent
all week," Tank muttered. Rosa put a hand on his arm, smiling. Zero
continued. "What remains after the cheering ends?

14
00:04:52,781 --> 00:05:09,376
What can Captain Aiden offer that an empire cannot?" I looked around
the room. At the officers who had been ordered to fire on their own
captains. At the palace workers standing near the doors because they
had not yet decided they were allowed to sit.

15
00:05:09,626 --> 00:05:30,112
At Roland in his torn white suit, alive because I had pulled him out
of the car Zero had sent men to shoot. Then I looked at my wife. She
did not nod. She did not tell me what answer would make me good. She
waited to hear me. "A ride home," I said. Zero frowned. "For who?"
"Whoever came with me.

16
00:05:30,362 --> 00:05:50,410
Whoever decides to leave with me. Whoever you keep telling can't go
until you're finished needing them. Nigga, I got a lot of cars. It's
not a complicated offer." A murmur moved through the seats. "And
afterward?" Zero asked. "Afterward I marry my wife again. My brother
gets married.

17
00:05:50,660 --> 00:06:14,925
We eat too much, spend too much, and wake up somewhere you can't call
to ruin the fucking morning." "A small ambition." "Nigga, you built
all this because nobody wanted to stay for breakfast. Don't talk to me
about ambition." The room went silent. Not polite silence. The kind
where everybody suddenly knows which sentence will be remembered if
the shooting starts. Zero's face changed.

18
00:06:15,175 --> 00:06:35,166
For a moment I saw the man beneath the emperor. Not wounded innocence.
Not some little boy a story could excuse into a throne. A grown man
who had spent years choosing to hurt people and still hated
discovering they might laugh at him. He looked at Shawna. Then at
Tank. Then at me.

19
00:06:35,416 --> 00:06:58,952
"I could have made you my heir." "Nigga, I already inherited enough
bad ideas." "The world would have opened to us." "It keeps opening
when I knock. You the nigga hiding behind doors." He drew his sword.
The sound ran through the court like a match being struck. I drew
mine. Knox sat forward, looking proud enough to make every officer
around her nervous.

20
00:06:59,202 --> 00:07:21,200
"Excellent purchase," she whispered. Shawna took the crown off my
head. I looked at her. "You don't want it scratched," she said.
"Nigga, priorities." She kissed me once, directly on the mouth, in
front of the emperor and every person he had invited to watch me fail.
Then she stepped back holding the crown in both hands. I climbed onto
the platform.

21
00:07:21,450 --> 00:07:44,395
Zero attacked before I reached the center. Fast. Hard. None of the
decorative bullshit I had expected from a man with that many
portraits. His blade struck mine with enough force to send pain
through my shoulder. I stepped back, turned the second strike, and
nearly lost my footing on the polished marble. The nigga had trained.
Good.

22
00:07:44,645 --> 00:08:03,626
I was tired of men confusing money with being able to swing a sword.
He pressed forward, driving me toward the platform's edge. The court
watched without breathing. I heard Tank shift in his seat. I heard
Rosa catch his wrist. "Stay," she whispered. Zero smiled.

23
00:08:03,876 --> 00:08:26,678
"Your friends are anxious." "Nigga, they got dinner reservations." I
turned his next strike, stepped inside the reach, and hit him with my
shoulder. The bruised one. Pain flashed white. But Zero went backward.
I followed, striking high, then low, making the nigga work for every
inch he had thought the throne would give him. His blade caught mine.

24
00:08:26,928 --> 00:08:49,592
We locked close enough for me to see sweat at his hairline. "You
should be exhausted," he said. "Nigga, I'm married. I learned
endurance." I shoved him away. The audience laughed. That cost him
more than the shove. He came at me harder. I let him spend it. Step
back. Turn. Strike. The sword in my hand felt heavy now, but I knew
heavy.

25
00:08:49,842 --> 00:09:10,323
I had carried money, bodies, grief, guns, my wife up a fucking palace
staircase. Weight had never been enough to persuade me I should put
down what I wanted. Zero cut my sleeve. A hot line opened along my
upper arm. Shawna's fingers tightened around the crown. I saw it. The
nigga saw me see it.

26
00:09:10,573 --> 00:09:28,105
He aimed the next strike toward her side of the court, making me turn
my body to block him from the edge. That was when he understood the
advantage he thought he had. "There," he whispered. He attacked toward
the seats. I met him before he could reach them. Our swords rang.

27
00:09:28,355 --> 00:09:51,196
I pushed him back onto the platform, furious now, and the fury made me
careless for half a second. He struck my wrist. My sword slipped. I
caught it lower, barely, and felt the hilt bite my palm. Zero smiled.
"Every man has a place he can be led." "Nigga," I said, "you keep
confusing love with a leash." I stepped forward instead of back.

28
00:09:51,446 --> 00:10:15,149
His eyes widened. I caught his blade against the side of mine, turned
beneath his arm, and drove my elbow into his ribs. He staggered. I
struck his wrist with the hilt. The sword flew from his hand and slid
across the platform. I put my blade against his throat. The court
rose. Every nigga in that room stood at once. Zero held still.

29
00:10:15,399 --> 00:10:36,756
For the first time, the emperor had no door between us. I could have
ended him there. Then a gunshot cracked from the upper seats. The
glass dome shattered. A section of the metal frame broke loose above
the lower row where Marcellus sat. I saw the old man look up. I moved
before the thought finished. I left Zero.

30
00:10:37,006 --> 00:10:59,111
I jumped from the platform, hit Marcellus's chair, and drove both of
us beneath the stone lip of the lower aisle as the frame crashed down
where his head had been. Glass filled the air. The court screamed.
Tank fired toward the upper seats. Knox's officers moved. Shawna
dropped behind the bench with the crown pressed to her chest.

31
00:10:59,361 --> 00:11:22,861
Vesper pulled Magnolia clear of the falling frame. Marcellus lay
beside me, stunned, his glasses crooked. "My case," he whispered.
"Nigga, your head first." I looked back at the platform. Zero was
gone. A door behind the throne stood open. The nigga had ordered his
own court shattered so he could escape the moment it saw him lose.

32
00:11:23,111 --> 00:11:46,705
Rage moved through the room faster than the gunfire. Noor's guards
turned on the Black Mantle shooters. Salma pulled the palace workers
into the lower aisle. Roland climbed the seats after a man who had
fired at us, caught him by the coat, and dragged him down before he
could reload. The emperor had invited witnesses. Now every witness had
seen enough.

33
00:11:46,955 --> 00:12:12,133
Shawna reached me with the crown under one arm. "Marcellus?" "Alive,"
the old man said, offended to be discussed while present. She touched
his cheek, then mine. My arm bled through the torn sleeve. "Aiden." "I
know." Tank came up beside us. "That nigga ran." I looked at the open
door behind the throne. "Then we finish moving." Shawna gave the crown
to Marcellus.

34
00:12:12,383 --> 00:12:27,947
He held it with both hands. "I will keep this safe," he said. I
nodded. Then I picked up my sword, took my wife's hand, and went after
the man who had finally run out of beautiful rooms where somebody else
could die for him.
